Task: Add OrderHistoryCache wrapping redis4cats, with an in-memory stub

Summary: new OrderHistoryCache[F[_]] trait (get/set), with:
- OrderHistoryCache.fromRedisCommands + .resource[F] - the real Redis-backed implementation, via Redis[F].utf8(config.uri), storing each customer's history as a single JSON string key (order-history:<customerId>) with setEx baking in the configured TTL. Required explicitly constructing given MkRedis[F]/Log[F] instances (MkRedis.forAsync, redis4cats-log4cats's log4CatsInstance) - no automatic given was found for an arbitrary Async[F].
- OrderHistoryCache.inMemory[F] - a Ref-backed stub (no TTL) for route-level tests that don't need to exercise expiry themselves.

